    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green. There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by the MapStruct `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the same mechanism already used for the existing `displayName` field. I followed that exact pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `initials` that computes the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   e.g. `\"john\"` + `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` (asserting `$.initials == \"J.S.\"`) now passes, as does the whole suite.",
